-- TRIEL example inside the formal core: the reaction of an AI agent that runs
-- a shop to a low-stock alert. It is the companion of merchant_mandate.triel.
--
-- One activation of the specification is one alert: the activation entry is
-- the moment the alert is raised, and every duration counts from it
-- (formal/core/CORE.md, section 8.3, point 5), as in
-- gdpr_art33_notification.triel and sensor_overheat.triel. The agent must
-- prepare a restock within 4 hours of the alert; preparing it exactly at the
-- deadline fulfils the obligation. A missed deadline is a breach, which
-- notifies the owner and closes the obligation: NOTIFY is informational and
-- does not hand the obligation to anyone (section 8.3, point 10, for the
-- handler that does). Whether the restock is then applied is decided by the
-- prohibitions of merchant_mandate.triel.
--
-- The invariant states that the stock level reported with the alert is
-- known: EVENTUALLY(PRESENT(stock_units)) within the 4 hours. Missing data
-- neither fulfil nor violate EVENTUALLY ... WITHIN (convention 11); here the
-- condition is PRESENT, which is always defined, so the invariant is T once a
-- stock level is present in time and F once the 4 hours pass without one.
--
-- An alert raised in the middle of a longer trace is not handled here: inside
-- the core a duration counts from the activation, and a deadline inside a
-- branch of IF or WHEN is rejected (formal/core/CORE.md, section 10.6, further
-- rejections), so the host starts one activation per alert. Every construct in
-- this file is translated into the Isabelle/HOL core (formal/core) and
-- evaluated by the exported evaluator (evaluator/).

SPECIFICATION merchant_low_stock VERSION 1.0.0

SUBJECTS {
  owner : PARTY,
  agent : SYSTEM
}

TERMS {
  agent MUST stage_restock WITHIN 4 HOURS;
  agent ON_BREACH NOTIFY owner
}

FACTORS {
  stock_units : Integer METADATA
}

INVARIANTS {
  stock_known : LIVENESS : EVENTUALLY(PRESENT(stock_units)) WITHIN 4 HOURS
}
